From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: no_trace <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ghosthook: commit emitted Ghost writes before EL0 exposure

The Ghost pages are written through the kernel direct mapping and later
installed as VMA-less executable EL0 mappings. Mark each producer update
non-clean at the point it occurs so arm64's set_pte_at() cache-synchronisation
path cannot inherit a clean indication from a recycled page.

The scalar emitter is specifically used by KPM-generated code. Use one aligned
WRITE_ONCE store for its register-carried word rather than a transient source
object, then mark the destination page dirty.

---
 mm/gh_ghost.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/gh_ghost.c b/mm/gh_ghost.c
index ffffffff..eeeeeeee 100644
--- a/mm/gh_ghost.c
+++ b/mm/gh_ghost.c
@@ -265,6 +265,10 @@ int gh_ghost_region_write(struct mm_struct *mm, u64 handle,
 		chunk = min_t(unsigned long, len, PAGE_SIZE - page_offset);
 		memcpy((u8 *)page_address(region->pages[page]) + page_offset, input,
 		       chunk);
+		/* The page may subsequently appear through a VMA-less EL0 alias.
+		 * Mark every producer write dirty now; set_pte_at() then owns the
+		 * architecture-specific clean/invalidate when RX is installed. */
+		flush_dcache_page(region->pages[page]);
 		offset += chunk;
 		input += chunk;
 		len -= chunk;
@@ -295,8 +299,12 @@ int gh_ghost_region_write_u32(struct mm_struct *mm, u64 handle,
 	}
 	page = offset >> PAGE_SHIFT;
 	page_offset = offset & ~PAGE_MASK;
-	memcpy((u8 *)page_address(region->pages[page]) + page_offset,
-	       &value, sizeof(value));
+	/* Do not route this four-byte emitter through a transient source buffer.
+	 * A single aligned store also makes the KPM ABI's register-carried value
+	 * explicit.  Record the page as dirty before it can be exposed at EL0. */
+	WRITE_ONCE(*(u32 *)((u8 *)page_address(region->pages[page]) +
+			      page_offset), value);
+	flush_dcache_page(region->pages[page]);
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&gh_ghost_lock);
 	return ret;
